<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  godot-cineform's own manifest. This repository is a `repo` manifest ROOT.

  WHY IT CARRIES ITS OWN MANIFEST RATHER THAN LEANING ON THE WORKSPACE ONE.
  This project needs two dependencies and nothing else does. Putting them in
  `weftspun/weftspun`'s default.xml made every checkout of the workspace fetch a C++ binding
  library and a video codec, whether or not anyone intended to build a GDExtension. It also
  placed them as siblings, where their relationship to this project was a comment rather than
  a path.

  Fetched HERE, into thirdparty/, the arrangement says what it is: these belong to this build.

  This manifest is STANDALONE. It includes no other manifest and is included by none, so a
  clone of this repository is enough to build it.

    repo init -u https://github.com/weftspun/godot-cineform -m default.xml
    repo sync

  NOT SUBMODULES, and CLAUDE.md blocklists those. A submodule pins a dependency in a file only
  git reads. `repo status` cannot see it, and a bump appears in a diff as a bare hash with no
  name, no branch and no reason. A manifest entry carries all three, plus room for the comment
  explaining the pin, which is what the entries below use.
-->
<manifest>
  <remote name="weftspun" fetch="https://github.com/weftspun" />
  <default remote="weftspun" sync-j="4" />

  <!-- Forked from godotengine/godot-cpp. Forked rather than pinned upstream because a
       `revision` on somebody else's repository is a promise they have not made.

       The commit is godot-whisper's, exactly. That project builds nine platform and
       architecture pairs from this tree, so any platform failure here is ours rather than a
       question about the binding library. It is branch 4.2, which sets the engine floor.

       Measured, not assumed: every method hash this extension binds is identical in Godot 4.0
       through 4.5, and gen_bindings.py fails the build if that stops being true. So 4.2 is a
       choice about which tree to trust, not a limit anyone found. -->
  <project name="godot-cpp" path="thirdparty/godot-cpp"
           revision="4bc6e67d51df4c12e150fe4769911e239c627a47" />

  <!-- Forked from gopro/cineform-sdk, for the same reason. Dual licensed
       `Apache-2.0 OR MIT`, which is this workspace's own pair, so nothing new enters an
       export. That licence is the reason this project exists rather than linking FFmpeg,
       which is LGPL and would follow every Godot export forever. RFD 0123 has the argument. -->
  <project name="cineform-sdk" path="thirdparty/cineform-sdk"
           revision="11574d0295771edccadd17af14af74a539f924c7" />
</manifest>
